#: ee7a18ede67b43ee8d41e4fc90782686
msgid "Test System"
msgstr "测试系统"

#: 3036c26a58524676a4245afa928e2adc
msgid "Status: Accepted"
msgstr ""

#: 0f2c4141dda64350ad989a3f0a8a72f6
msgid "Last reviewed: 2026-08-12"
msgstr ""

#: 600ef13bf1d34f67aa6a16372f65a196
msgid "Baseline: `582fc51d`"
msgstr ""

#: 0bc7f960032541b19abd51093b43313e
msgid "Owner: test infrastructure maintainers"
msgstr ""

#: e8ecc16d3f8b4f2fa48080c28de6cf3a
msgid ""
"Review when: collection roots, markers, OpInfo contracts, or backend "
"gates change"
msgstr ""

#: ffc14f2746e745d9a118b66f82c2129a
msgid ""
"Jittor uses pytest as the repository test runner while retaining "
"compatible `unittest.TestCase` tests. The suite lives under root `tests/`"
" and is not part of the installed package. "
"[`pyproject.toml`](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/pyproject.toml)"
" is the authoritative collection and marker configuration; "
"[`noxfile.py`](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/noxfile.py) "
"is the reproducible command surface."
msgstr ""

#: 217564e627df480f8d39bfe15236bf8b
msgid "Goals"
msgstr ""

#: 40f8842d0c934cab9d776112fa212ddd
msgid "Compare forward behavior with an independent reference."
msgstr ""

#: c1e41f9445d44ec0bd9c0a4d6696d48d
msgid "Verify analytical gradients numerically and across devices."
msgstr ""

#: 7d646285317e400db4f5d47d6a8c4c28
msgid "Keep structure, CPU, and hardware requirements explicit."
msgstr ""

#: 2739c331e9ae46fe81cc827fde0299e2
msgid ""
"Preserve useful legacy edge cases while replacing cross-test imports and "
"ad-hoc discovery with shared helpers and registries."
msgstr ""

#: b933f282674d4799882800bd4309f77d
msgid ""
"Make unsupported behavior visible through specific skips or strict "
"expected failures."
msgstr ""

#: de36ccc042484457a78d233f400c09e4
msgid "Keep collection free of compilation, downloads, and hardware side effects."
msgstr ""

#: ba04b0be284b431187981dd8027a9bce
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: 69958cc7b4d1469693baad720eed01ab
msgid ""
"Test modules may import `tests/_helpers` and `tests/opinfo` through the "
"pytest Python path configured for the suite. They must not import another"
" test module as an implicit helper API. Shared utilities need their own "
"focused tests when they contain nontrivial comparison or device logic."
msgstr ""

#: 2727a2c05e474f0fb1d3449c54bb36f2
msgid "Three layers of operator evidence"
msgstr ""

#: c5587e92691d460fa2430dca2333f9a0
msgid "1. Independent forward reference"
msgstr ""

#: 04c66b1ed22941f8bec89dbada8dd5d3
msgid ""
"Each `OpInfo` describes the callable, sample builder, dtypes, autograd "
"support, tolerances, and targeted skip/xfail policy. "
"`tests/ops/test_ops.py` expands the database across requested devices and"
" compares outputs with independent NumPy or mathematical references."
msgstr ""

#: fdfc62f5ab604306a7f2bc66e9d7274d
msgid ""
"The reference must not call the Jittor operation under test. Sample "
"builders cover meaningful shapes, axes, broadcasting, optional arguments,"
" and error-prone dtypes rather than generating volume without semantic "
"variety."
msgstr ""

#: 7820cf05cc564192a6d6af295ffcf57d
msgid "2. Numerical gradients"
msgstr ""

#: 00cdc4ae7eec47419f1adff621e6a61f
msgid ""
"Differentiable OpInfo entries run float64 CPU `gradcheck`; operations "
"that support second-order differentiation also run `gradgradcheck`. "
"Marking `supports_autograd=False` or `supports_gradgrad=False` is a "
"contract decision, not a way to make a failing test green, and requires a"
" reason in the definition or known-issues ledger."
msgstr ""

#: 05812065de19467cbcf7ef73af1a03f5
msgid ""
"Numerical checks prove derivative formulas on CPU. They do not prove that"
" an accelerator executes the same backward kernel correctly."
msgstr ""

#: 7a9ff21baa3c4e95bee5a36d5c33d465
msgid "3. Device parity"
msgstr ""

#: 2680ca51fa5c47b28d7fb0479cd5be97
msgid ""
"[`tests/backends/parity/test_device_parity.py`](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/tests/backends/parity/test_device_parity.py)"
" runs identical inputs and cotangents on CPU and the available "
"accelerator, comparing forward outputs and gradients with both global and"
" per-element error metrics. This layer catches device-specific compile "
"failures, dropped gradient contributions, and silent kernel divergence."
msgstr ""

#: d56391d9d41e42e0a29d65fa53bfcdfd
msgid ""
"CPU is a practical parity oracle only after its behavior is independently"
" pinned by the forward and numerical-gradient layers. Backend environment"
" failures are reported separately from framework defects."
msgstr ""

#: ab1ca150bb60423d91ec1f5eb918f11d
msgid "Test categories and markers"
msgstr ""

#: e03fccd8e06444d9b9c65a37feb8d104
msgid ""
"Markers are registered in "
"[`pyproject.toml`](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/pyproject.toml):"
msgstr ""

#: cc64857bc5fe4dad80f6d7e345a565ac
msgid "Marker"
msgstr ""

#: db6c1ccfcced42bca395aa7ea49486a3
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: 454229836f1944d48f1242224c62e4ae
msgid "`structure`"
msgstr ""

#: b23b5b2d0e1b405b961f09b9f4df8da0
msgid "no device execution; layout, packaging, and static checks"
msgstr ""

#: e6487abd6a464501a3ae743ffda1b9f9
msgid "`cpu`"
msgstr ""

#: cfa3bbc321384314b5c2013523e9fa49
msgid "maintained CPU behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ee3de24b1a664d71b172bccc712b3fb9
msgid "`cuda`"
msgstr ""

#: 6b7a51d806bf425a9367785018caad6d
msgid "requires an NVIDIA CUDA environment"
msgstr ""

#: 60626ad81ca44d90afc26688fc150e6b
msgid "`rocm`"
msgstr ""

#: 359eadd82b084246a90785355074b155
msgid "requires an AMD ROCm environment"
msgstr ""

#: f95947accdaa44029d1fea181603ecb3
msgid "`npu`"
msgstr ""

#: ec25c2b6fc944b0ca8c01fc68ac92297
msgid "requires an Ascend CANN environment"
msgstr ""

#: a0a1dbfe78004308a921919c4edab70f
msgid "`mpi`"
msgstr ""

#: b1090112e6754e39bf424647a6b81051
msgid "requires an MPI launcher or multiple processes"
msgstr ""

#: 3b55cfa0ee404d4d8eb0f49d1e4597c2
msgid "`slow`"
msgstr ""

#: d8cede27adc44cdeac9a04d9e502f3d1
msgid "excluded from the fast pull-request gate"
msgstr ""

#: 443aceda8f0242b68d0cfc434c1c055c
msgid "`network`"
msgstr ""

#: 3d4ddaf9c2184cda89dbab2060ce7cf0
msgid "requires external network access"
msgstr ""

#: 6b03aa2dcd914048a8fb75c1c46ce42e
msgid "`manual`"
msgstr ""

#: 0961f59e40e64f579f8db5cef9d93a97
msgid "selected explicitly; never part of automatic default runs"
msgstr ""

#: 424daffad02842968802a29b86e665b0
msgid ""
"Apply the narrowest applicable marker. Hardware tests probe a real "
"operation and must not silently pass on CPU. Network and manual tests "
"explain their external requirements in the module docstring."
msgstr ""

#: 61d9b8e5e1244a1ab82a1eb9d1dd79b0
msgid "Skips and known failures"
msgstr ""

#: ec92e637b8ef4311a4fde22a9973f148
msgid ""
"A skip represents an unavailable prerequisite or an intentionally "
"unsupported contract. Its reason identifies the exact prerequisite or "
"limitation."
msgstr ""

#: e0b6e83c7ab84472aa111c15ff171fff
msgid ""
"An expected failure represents a reproduced framework defect. Pytest uses"
" strict xfail behavior, so a fix produces an XPASS and forces ledger "
"cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: 60fe3b30f1a7450399c6d8755f8c5c88
msgid ""
"Do not catch arbitrary exceptions around a test body and convert them to "
"a skip. Probe optional environments narrowly before execution."
msgstr ""

#: bb94ddffc1f84175a8789eb183afe8ef
msgid ""
"Every persistent expected failure is listed in the [known-issues "
"ledger](https://github.com/Jittor/jittor/blob/master/agent/manuals/known-"
"issues.md) with an owner and an exit condition."
msgstr ""

#: f9b300382a354df88e2ad0c3d74cac67
msgid "Commands"
msgstr ""

#: 17ab215efad041a7865446c6a006472d
msgid ""
"The nox sessions create isolated state and caches. Direct concurrent runs"
" must also use distinct `JITTOR_HOME` or `cache_name` values. The first "
"build of a new JIT operation or extension should run serially."
msgstr ""

#: 4a8a74c891c94304bc68aa155b3c3241
msgid "Adding coverage"
msgstr ""

#: 55094a071db648f5a1c8cc7af3701875
msgid ""
"Use an OpInfo definition when one operation can share the standard "
"sample, reference, dtype, gradient, and device-parity machinery. Use a "
"focused test when the contract concerns state, mutation, serialization, "
"error behavior, module lifecycle, import order, distributed coordination,"
" or a specific regression not expressible through OpInfo."
msgstr ""

#: 798702ca7b6e40f48d9ea47a7845a3d7
msgid "A new operation normally needs:"
msgstr ""

#: e582ff9dd495478f8fed4cdf59a7a888
msgid "independent forward samples and reference;"
msgstr ""

#: 6a1aa38326764386ba00de2bf6bef329
msgid ""
"dtype, shape, axis, empty, broadcast, and non-contiguous cases as "
"applicable;"
msgstr ""

#: d3c97aa39fb54bbd931c948728e0e521
msgid "gradient and grad-gradient declarations backed by tests;"
msgstr ""

#: ce44a7c863174e30b60c5f73856ce204
msgid "device parity for every advertised accelerator;"
msgstr ""

#: 43aa58636ce7468b9c106675a1871953
msgid "explicit error-contract tests;"
msgstr ""

#: 9adca3cc86974a0588a9dd49c85e0c9b
msgid ""
"an OpInfo report entry or focused test name that makes missing coverage "
"discoverable."
msgstr ""

#: 3c63a0d1add54f61b993e96990b020af
msgid "Acceptance"
msgstr ""

#: 667923d7e20d4b9fb0345e79767b2282
msgid ""
"A test-system change is complete when collection succeeds without device "
"side effects, focused self-tests cover new harness logic, the structure "
"gate passes, at least one mandatory CPU case executes, and each hardware "
"result distinguishes pass, framework failure, and unavailable "
"environment. Counts alone are not an acceptance criterion; the evidence "
"must exercise the claimed semantics."
msgstr ""
